# Pensive Professor (0/2) with increment: the comparison is made again as the ability resolves (CR 603.4, the rulings). Bot1
# casts a one-mana Lightning Bolt (1 > power 0: increment triggers), then in response a one-mana Giant Growth, which
# triggers increment too (1 > 0). The Giant Growth's trigger resolves first and puts the one counter (1/3), drawing a card;
# Giant Growth makes it 4/6; when the Bolt's increment ability resolves 1 is greater than neither 4 nor 6, so it does
# nothing: one counter in all, one card drawn.

[Bot1 Deck]
Pensive Professor
Mox Sapphire x2
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Lightning Bolt
Giant Growth
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Pensive Professor.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Hand.Count = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Giant Growth.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Pensive Professor)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 17
Bot1.Hand.Count = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Pensive Professor.Power = 4
Bot1.Battlefield.Pensive Professor.Toughness = 6
Bot1.Battlefield.Pensive Professor.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
